---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
        title="Systems — CivicBrands"
        description="The CivicBrands public infrastructure set: KC directory, Forecast, Open Cognition, research, artifacts, and procurement records."
>
    <section class="section">
        <p class="eyebrow">Systems</p>

        <div class="measure">
            <h1>The set is the signal.</h1>
            <p>
                CivicBrands is not one product. It is a public infrastructure practice: directories,
                observational systems, governed memory patterns, records, comments, and procurement
                material built so people can inspect the systems that act on them.
            </p>
            <p>
                The work shares one posture: make the structure legible, preserve the record, keep
                agency attached to the people inside the process.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid system-grid">
            <a class="route-panel" href="/kc">
                <p class="eyebrow">KC Directory</p>
                <h2 class="card-title">Survival and navigation resources across the bi-state metro.</h2>
                <p>People-first resource infrastructure with cross-service navigation, exports, corrections, and plain-language access notes.</p>
            </a>

            <a class="route-panel" href="https://forecast.civicbrands.org">
                <p class="eyebrow">Forecast</p>
                <h2 class="card-title">Time-resolved observational field infrastructure.</h2>
                <p>Environmental and civic observations preserved with source fidelity, geography, and temporal integrity.</p>
            </a>

            <a class="route-panel" href="/work/open-cognition">
                <p class="eyebrow">Open Cognition</p>
                <h2 class="card-title">Reference substrate for governed agent memory.</h2>
                <p>Patterns for immutable canonical objects, scoped references, stop lifecycle, and accountable memory state.</p>
            </a>

            <a class="route-panel" href="/research">
                <p class="eyebrow">Research</p>
                <h2 class="card-title">Analysis that gives the systems a language.</h2>
                <p>Frames for abstraction harm, situated inference, record sufficiency, and institutional legibility.</p>
            </a>

            <a class="route-panel" href="/artifacts">
                <p class="eyebrow">Artifacts</p>
                <h2 class="card-title">Records that remain inspectable.</h2>
                <p>Public comments, matrices, entity records, and documents intended to survive outside a feed.</p>
            </a>

            <a class="route-panel" href="/procurement">
                <p class="eyebrow">Procurement</p>
                <h2 class="card-title">The institutional doorway.</h2>
                <p>Entity facts, capability areas, contacts, and readiness material for public-sector and civic partners.</p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>
</BaseLayout>
